2.1 Introduction

Requirement Analysis identifies the hardware, software, technologies, and functional capabilities needed to develop and operate the ComicCraft application.

The system is designed using Python, FastAPI, Gemini AI models, Stable Diffusion, HTML, CSS, and Jinja2.

2.2 Functional Requirements

The system should allow users to enter a story prompt.

The system should accept a character name and story setting.

The system should allow users to select the story tone and art style.

The system should generate a structured five-panel comic outline.

The system should generate narration and character dialogues.

The system should create illustrations for each comic panel.

The system should display the generated comic on a preview page.

The system should organize the panels into a structured layout.

The system should generate a downloadable PDF.

The system should provide appropriate error messages if an operation fails.

2.3 Non-Functional Requirements

Usability: The interface should be simple and easy to understand.

Performance: The application should process requests efficiently, subject to AI model response times.

Reliability: The system should handle API errors and invalid inputs appropriately.

Maintainability: The source code should be organized into separate modules.

Scalability: The modular architecture should support future improvements.

Security: API keys and access tokens should be stored securely.

Compatibility: The web interface should be accessible through commonly used browsers.

